.tur-abi-cache/

# `tur emit-c` / `tur emit-h` output, checked in by accident.
#
# These 14 files carry a "/* generated by tur (phase 2) */" banner and nothing
# reads them: a build emits fresh C into $TMPDIR/tur-build and never looks
# here.  They are also wrong -- they were generated while the spice could not
# compile (raygui.h was never on the include path, so every Gui* call fell
# through to an implicit declaration), so what is captured in them is the
# broken elaboration, not the current one.  Same reasoning as tur.lock and
# cmake/: a stale generated artifact in the tree is worse than no artifact,
# because it looks authoritative.
raygui__*.c
raygui__*.h

# `tur fetch` writes both of these, each stamped "AUTO-GENERATED ... Do not
# edit"; see the repo-root .gitignore for the full reasoning.
cmake/CMakeLists.txt
cmake/spice-deps-manifest.json
